            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          },
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582783,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Heraclitus's Life</strong><br>\nHeraclitus was an ancient Greek philosopher born in Ephesus, a city on the coast of Ionia. Around 500 BCE, his works contributed significantly to the philosophical concept of change being the fundamental essence of the universe. Known as the \"weeping philosopher\" for his critical view of humanity, Heraclitus believed most people failed to see the underlying truths of the world.</p>\n\n<p><strong>The Philosophy of Change</strong><br>\nHeraclitus famously said, \"No man ever steps in the same river twice,\" illustrating his belief that change is constant. To him, the universe is in a perpetual state of flux. He saw change as a reality that manifests in cycles, where fire played a central role as an element that transforms other elements through its essence.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Logos and Universal Reason</strong><br>\nHeraclitus introduced the concept of the Logos, a universal guiding principle that governs all changes and transformations. He believed that although Logos is omnipresent and always at work, people are unable to understand it fully because they do not use their faculties to see the order of things.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "53bc5361-5ce5-43a9-a00f-57bbceee9cd0"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          }
        ],
