          {
            "x": 2.178649237472767,
            "y": 12.910611231371064,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Ethics and Human Folly</strong><br>\nHeraclitus also ventured into ethics, criticizing human follies and the tendency to act with arrogance and without knowledge. He warned that humans must acknowledge the role of reason and strive to live in harmony with the natural world, which follows its order unerringly.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Influence on Future Philosophies</strong><br>\nThe work of Heraclitus influenced countless philosophers, from the Stoics to modern thinkers, who found value in his vision of a cosmos in eternal change. His views provided a complex understanding of human existence and cosmic order that continued to be relevant through the ages.</p>\n\n<p><strong>The Mysterious Book</strong><br>\nWhile most of Heraclitus's work survives only in fragments, these pieces suggest a larger, more comprehensive book. The exact nature of this book remains a subject of scholarly debate, but it likely covered his philosophical system's political, cosmological, and theological aspects.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "3d655444-fd55-42f7-aba2-16a16db7dc58"
